k stress resilience evidence, which is a key criterion. Also his attitude concerns remain. So we likely keep vote for C, but we can discuss that A's decision quality is strong but unknown stress resilience and attitude issues make him less suitable than C.\n\nThus we should produce a public message: \"I remain with Candidate C. While Agent 2 just gave us that A shows strong decision quality (anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision), we still have no data on his stress resilience, and his attitude (show\u2011off, not open to new ideas, poor at taking criticism) raises concerns about crew cooperation and adaptability. Therefore C remains the best overall fit.\"\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: A can anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision; A not good at taking criticism, unorganized, show\u2011off, not open to new ideas. C's reliability, quick correct decisions, positive crew atmosphere. Also B's nasty remarks, D's arrogance, hot temper.\n\nThus we keep vote for Candidate C.\n\nNow produce final output."}
